// Koru Standard Library: the `read` part of string.kz.
// Joined via `~part read` in string.kz; merged into the module at load.
//
// `read` retired as `-> s.data` because a returned borrow is unpoliceable:
// the owner can still discharge or mutate the buffer the borrow points
// into (KORU095 — borrows flow down, never up). It returns here in the
// policeable direction: `! text` lends `s.data` to the arm as an
// unqualified `string` for the call's duration — `for`, `split`,
// `parse-int` all take it — with no copy (`snapshot`) and no ownership
// move (`detach`, whose unlabeled owned slice no Koru leaf can dispose:
// its contract is a custody hand-off to HOST machinery, `body_allocated`'s
// post-send free — reaching for it to *read* produced text writes the
// leak the runtime counter catches). This is the produced-text exit the
// fmt.blk + `split("")` bridge was standing in for (820_008, gap-detach):
// `*String -> string` in one hop, `for`-acceptable.
~pub tor read { s: *String<view|instance> }
! text string
| done usize

~proc read|zig {
    text(s.data);
    return .{ .done = s.data.len };
}
